user_message:
Review every unordered pair in this JSON feature list. Use its local zero-based indices,
not hypothesis IDs. Preserve all feature fields when deciding measurement equivalence.

[
  {
    "hypothesis_id": 26,
    "feature": {
      "name": "any_comment_acknowledges_premise_before_divergence",
      "dtype": "binary",
      "source_columns": [
        "title",
        "argument",
        "OC_comments"
      ],
      "definition": "OC_comments (other users' counter-argument comments, not OP) judged against the OP's title and argument: 1 if at least one comment explicitly acknowledges the validity of the OP's initial premise (stated in title/argument) and then, later within the same comment, introduces a disagreement or divergent point; else 0.",
      "kind": "prompt",
      "spec": "Read the OP's title and argument (to identify the OP's initial premise) and each comment in the OC_comments JSON list (written by other users; list order is not chronology). Emit 1 if at least one comment contains an explicit statement that the OP's initial premise (or a core starting assumption stated in the title/argument) is valid, correct, reasonable, or fair (e.g. 'you're right that...', 'that's a fair point'), AND afterwards in the same comment introduces a disagreement, qualification, or alternative that diverges from the OP's conclusion. The acknowledgment must be explicit and about the OP's premise, not mere politeness, generic praise, or acknowledging only a side detail; it must precede the divergence in the comment text. Quoted text attributed to others doesn't count as acknowledgment by the commenter. Emit 0 if comments are parsed and none qualify (including an empty list). Emit null if OC_comments is malformed or the title/argument is missing so the premise cannot be identified. Do not use the conversation column or later replies."
    }
  },
  {
    "hypothesis_id": 60,
    "feature": {
      "name": "any_comment_acknowledges_component_then_counterexample",
      "dtype": "binary",
      "source_columns": [
        "title",
        "argument",
        "OC_comments"
      ],
      "definition": "OC_comments (other users' comments only, not OP): 1 if at least one comment explicitly acknowledges the validity of a specific component of the OP's original argument (title/argument) and then presents a counter-example, else 0.",
      "kind": "prompt",
      "spec": "Read title and argument (the OP's view) and every comment in OC_comments (JSON list of comments by other users; order carries no meaning; ignore conversation and later replies). Emit 1 if at least one single comment (a) explicitly states that some specific identifiable part of the OP's argument or premise is valid/correct/fair (e.g. 'you're right that X', 'X is true'), where X is a specific component rather than a vague general politeness or 'good post', and (b) afterwards in the same comment presents a counter-example (a concrete case or instance that challenges the OP's view or claim). The acknowledgment must come before the counter-example in the comment text. Acknowledging only in a quoted/restated way without endorsement, generic politeness, acknowledgment without any counter-example, or counter-example without prior specific acknowledgment do not qualify. Emit 0 if the list is complete and parseable but no comment qualifies, including an empty list. Emit null if OC_comments cannot be parsed or title/argument are missing."
    }
  },
  {
    "hypothesis_id": 85,
    "feature": {
      "name": "any_acknowledge_then_narrow_caveat",
      "dtype": "binary",
      "source_columns": [
        "OC_comments",
        "title",
        "argument"
      ],
      "definition": "Other users' comments in OC_comments (not OP, not conversation): 1 if at least one comment first explicitly acknowledges some validity/correctness of the OP's view or point and then introduces a narrower, specific caveat, exception or qualification; else 0.",
      "kind": "prompt",
      "spec": "Read title and argument for the OP's view, then each comment in the OC_comments JSON list (comments by other users; list order is not chronology; ignore conversation). Emit 1 if at least one comment opens (before its caveat) with an explicit statement that the OP's view or a part of it is valid/reasonable/correct (e.g. 'you're right that...', 'this is true in general'), and afterwards raises a specific, limited caveat, exception or qualification rather than rejecting the whole view. Mere politeness, thanks or a quoted restatement without conceding validity do not count. Emit 0 if comments are assessable and none match. Null if OC_comments is empty/unparseable or title/argument missing."
    }
  }
]

Submit {"comparisons": [...]} covering every pair with an explicit verdict and reason.
